{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Favor.</b> From the root of compassion; from it too is תחנה (supplication). Its pattern is like קץ, and both are from doubled stems. The sense is the finding of favor, like \"no eye spared you\" (Ezekiel 16:5)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "I read מפעלי הכפל as referring to both חן and תחנה belonging to doubled/geminated root paradigms; the phrasing is compressed and the exact grammatical argument is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:28.088351294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}